## Project 3 — System Impact Analyzer

### Implementation checkpoint — 6 October 2026

The first brew-temperature scenario was implemented with nine synthetic
entities across six types, explicit relationship semantics, a bounded traversal policy,
and one shortest explanation path per candidate. It includes a command-line
demo and a local browser interface with a change form, grouped engineering and
documentation candidates, and expandable paths. The steam branch demonstrates
that unrelated entities stay outside the brew results.

Nine engine tests and four HTTP integration tests cover the current milestone.
See [the first scenario](first-working-scenario.md) for adopted model decisions
and [the README](../README.md) for run instructions. The broader phases below
remain the project plan; their larger example datasets and UI concepts are not
all implemented.

Phases 1–9 are complete for the bounded first scenario. The
[portfolio case study](portfolio-case-study.md) completes the Phase 10 narrative
with the implemented model, review behaviour, validation, lessons, and limits.
The demo meets the finish line below. The [second engineering scenario](second-working-scenario.md) is also
implemented: brew pressure uses a separate engineering branch and shares one
documentation topic with temperature regulation. The dataset now has 15 entities
and 13 relationships across six types. Both engineering scenarios return six
review candidates; their only shared candidate is the specification topic.

**Core question:**

> **When one thing in a complex product changes, what else might require review?**

**Domain:** fictional industrial coffee machine.

**Primary demonstration:** ontology + knowledge graph + relationship traversal + technical-documentation impact analysis.

**Not:** another chatbot, search engine, repository cleanup tool, or engineering simulator.

